dict(id='B36', act=7, set='marble', vis='Marble hall, a dollar bill on a pedestal beside a gold bar under glass. The gold bar slides away. Tag: AUG 15, 1971.',
  lines=[('N', "The dollar used to be tied to gold. In August nineteen seventy-one, President Nixon cut that link. Since then the dollar has been backed by one thing: trust. Trust that the government will keep it stable, and that the Federal Reserve won't let too much or too little of it slosh around. Print too much and prices run away. Keep too little and the economy chokes. Money is an agreement. And like any agreement, it only lasts as long as people keep believing in it.")]),
